  "name": "XNAT",
  "alternateName": [
    "XNAT Imaging Informatics Platform"
  ],
  "description": "Open-source biomedical imaging informatics platform developed by the Neuroinformatics Research Group (NRG) at Washington University School of Medicine. Provides end-to-end management of medical imaging data: DICOM ingestion and anonymisation, quality control, automated pipeline processing (container service, HPC integration), integrated search across imaging and clinical metadata, and secure multi-site data sharing with granular role-based access controls. Widely deployed across academic medical centres, national biobanks, and multi-site clinical research consortia globally. Modular architecture supports extensions via plugins; XNAT Works offers a commercial hosted and supported offering built on the open-source core.",
